# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env.
#
# Generate a token with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# Paste the same value into the desktop app under Settings → Data source.
AGENT_TOKEN=__CHANGE_ME_AGENT__

# Everything below has a working default and only needs setting on an unusual
# layout. See README.md for the full table.

# AGENT_PORT=8787
# AGENT_PHOTOS_PATH=/srv/photos
# AGENT_CLOUD_PATH=/srv/cloud
# Containers to report on, as `slug` or `slug=container`. Use the explicit form:
# neither stack's names are guessable, and a substring match cannot tell
# `immich_server` from `immich_machine_learning`. The slug is what the app shows;
# the container is what `docker ps` calls it.
# AGENT_SERVICES=immich=immich_server,nextcloud=nextcloud,mariadb=nextcloud-db,postgres=immich_postgres
# RESTIC_REPOSITORY=b2:filesynapse-backup:/
# The backup timer's verdict file. Read when it exists, so lastRunOk is a fact
# rather than an inference — see "Where lastRunOk comes from" in README.md.
# AGENT_BACKUP_STATUS=/var/lib/filesynapse/last-backup

# The wrapper provisioning installs, which "Back up now" in the app runs when it
# is present: it dumps both databases before snapshoting anything, then writes
# the verdict file above. Without it the agent falls back to calling restic
# directly — folders only, no databases — and says so in its log.
# AGENT_BACKUP_WRAPPER=/usr/local/bin/filesynapse-backup

# ── Where the libraries actually are on this host ───────────────────────────
#
# Only needed if provisioning put them somewhere other than /srv — it takes
# PHOTOS_DIR and FILES_DIR, and a machine with its own data disk will have moved
# them. Without these the agent mounts /srv, measures a directory nothing writes
# to, and reports disk usage for the wrong disk. That is the harder mistake to
# notice, because it reports a number rather than failing.
#
# The container-side paths do not change: the agent always sees /srv/photos and
# /srv/cloud.
# HOST_PHOTOS_DIR=/srv/photos
# HOST_CLOUD_DIR=/srv/cloud

# ── Optional decision pipeline ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Off unless you set it up. Leave everything below unset and the four
# /api/decisions routes answer "unavailable" without contacting anything; the
# app's Settings toggle then says so rather than failing.
#
# Immich's own ML container already does semantic search and face grouping, so
# this is an extra, not a replacement — see filesynapsetodo.md before enabling it, as
# moondream wants about 2 GB of RAM on a machine that is already busy.
#
# Laya, the decision model, is built from ./layla and started by the `decisions`
# profile alongside Ollama. Its image is large — torch plus a checkpoint — and it
# has never actually been built; see filesynapsetodo.md §8. Without it the cull queue
# still works and the album suggestion row simply does not render.

# Same compose stack, so these resolve by service name as written.
# AGENT_OLLAMA_URL=http://ollama:11434
# AGENT_LAYLA_URL=http://layla:8080

# Immich is in the *other* compose stack, so this one has no service name to
# assume. Pick whichever matches how you run it:
#   - if the agent joins the filesynapse network:
#       AGENT_IMMICH_URL=http://immich-server:2283
#   - otherwise, the host's own Tailscale address:
#       AGENT_IMMICH_URL=http://filesynapse:2283
AGENT_IMMICH_URL=

# The same all-scoped Immich key the desktop app uses (see filesynapsetodo.md §6 — a
# narrower-scoped key returns 403 from every metadata route).
AGENT_IMMICH_API_KEY=

# AGENT_VISION_MODEL=moondream
# Photos scored per request. The client loops until the queue drains, so this is
# a patience setting rather than a limit. Keep it small on a slow CPU.
# AGENT_DECISION_BATCH=8

# ── Memory caps ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Both containers are capped, because this box is also running Immich's own ML
# container and an uncapped model is how it ends up in swap. The failure mode of
# a cap set too low is a refused load, which is visible; the failure mode of no
# cap is a swap stall that takes the whole stack down, which is not.
#
# Raise OLLAMA_MEMORY if the model will not load — moondream needs roughly 2 GB.
# AGENT_MEMORY=512m
# OLLAMA_MEMORY=3g
